# Split pipe clamp as a small assembly: the lower jaw machined, the upper jaw a turned copy of
# it with a gap, a welded foot combined in, two cap screws as bodies of their own, copied, that
# cut their own seats in both jaws and stay.
bore = 40
gap = 1
lower: extrude sym 30 xz rect -50 -28 100 28
seat: extrude cut sym 30 xz circle 0 0 bore/2
fillet 4 (edges of lower along +z)
chamfer 1 (edges of seat)
upper: copybody rot 0 0 0 1 0 0 180 by 0 0 gap in lower
foot: extrude new 8 xy at 0 0 -36 rect -70 -25 140 50
fhole: hole 9 -xy at -60 -15 -28 thru in foot
pattern fhole lin 1 0 0 2 120 0 1 0 2 30
combine add lower foot
fillet 3 (edges between lower foot concave)
# the screw from head and shank (TODO: one revolve, revolve new xz at -37 0 gap+28 axis 0 0 0 1 poly 0 0 8 0 8 10 5 10 5 -50 0 -50, once regression revolve_cut_shoulder_on_face holds)
bolt: extrude new 10 xy at -37 0 gap+28 circle 0 0 8
shank: extrude new 50 xy at -37 0 gap+28-50 circle 0 0 5
combine add bolt shank
bolt2: copybody by 74 0 0 in bolt
combine cut upper bolt bolt2 keep
combine cut lower bolt bolt2 keep
